gsipper (1.2.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop G.729 / G.726 / G.723.1 from the codec set. Account >
    Advanced > Codecs now only shows Opus, G.722, G.722.1, G.711
    a-law / µ-law and GSM. _sanitize_codecs strips the retired
    codec ids out of any settings.json carried over from earlier
    1.2.x versions, so the UI is clean after upgrade with no
    manual edits.
  * build.sh: libbcg729-dev removed from PJ_BUILD_DEPS, and the
    pjproject configure line passes --disable-bcg729. The
    resulting _pjsua2.so has no DT_NEEDED entry for libbcg729 at
    all, so the deb no longer needs to recommend libbcg729-0.
  * debian/control.in: libbcg729-0 dropped from Recommends.
  * debian/postinst: the libbcg729-targeted hint is gone; only
    the generic 'sudo gsipper --install-pjsua2' fallback remains
    for any other pjsua2 import error.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.2.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * './build.sh --pjsua2' now FORCES a rebuild. Previously it
    short-circuited when 'import pjsua2' already worked, so a
    user upgrading from an older pjsua2 build (e.g. 2.14.1 with
    only G.722 compiled in) couldn't pick up the newer pjproject
    + bcg729 / opus link flags that ship in 1.2.x. The forced
    path also clears ~/.local/lib/python3*/site-packages/pjsua2*
    and the ~/.cache/gsipper/pjproject-* build tree so the
    rebuild is genuinely fresh. The implicit path (just running
    './build.sh') still only builds when nothing is there yet.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix pjlib SIGABRT when opening Account > Advanced. 1.2.3 added
    SipEndpoint.available_codec_ids(), which called pjsua2's
    codecEnum2() from the GTK main thread when the dialog opened.
    pjlib only allows calls from threads it knows about (the one
    that ran libCreate, plus its own internal workers), so the GTK
    thread tripped the 'Calling pjlib from unknown/external
    thread' assertion and the process aborted right after
    REGISTER succeeded.
    The codec list is now snapshotted on the SIP worker thread
    right after ep.libStart() (it's a stable list — codecs don't
    appear or disappear at runtime), and available_codec_ids()
    just returns the cached copy. No more pjlib traffic from GTK.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libbcg729-0 is now a Recommends, not a Depends — gsipper no
    longer refuses to install on machines that don't have it. With
    libbcg729-0 installed (the default on apt install), G.729 works
    as before. Without it, the bundled pjsua2 module fails to load
    and the existing PJSUA2_IMPORT_ERROR / 'offline' tooltip kicks
    in (gsipper still starts, just can't place calls until either
    libbcg729-0 is installed or pjsua2 is rebuilt without bcg729).
  * postinst now grep's the pjsua2 import error and gives a
    targeted hint: 'sudo apt install libbcg729-0' if that's what's
    missing, vs. the generic 'sudo gsipper --install-pjsua2' for
    anything else.
  * G.729 is OFF by default in the codec list. Account > Advanced >
    Codecs now grays out any codec that pjsua2's codecEnum2() does
    not report as available — its switch is set inactive, the row
    has a 'not available in this build' subtitle and a dim-label
    style, and the saved-settings 'enabled' bit is cleared so it
    doesn't leak back later. When the .so does support G.729 (the
    standard case with libbcg729-0 installed) the row behaves
    exactly as before — the user just toggles it on.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

