gsipper (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 'Start minimized' actually keeps the window hidden on first
    launch. HANDLES_COMMAND_LINE routes the initial activation
    through _on_command_line, which unconditionally called
    window.present(); do_activate (where the start_minimized check
    used to live) was bypassed. The check now runs in
    _on_command_line on first launch, distinguished from later
    invocations (Show from tray, app-grid re-launch) which still
    bring the window back.
  * Persist window size across hide / show cycles.
    GeneralSettings.window_width / window_height are written on
    every X-button close and applied via set_default_size in
    MainWindow.__init__. GTK4 / Wayland does not let apps restore
    window POSITION (the compositor decides), but size is now
    stable across sessions.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Status-menu Connect / Reconnect now also flip 'Account > Enabled'
    back on if it had been toggled off there. Previously, if the
    user disabled the account in Account settings, the status dot
    menu's Connect would call set_registration(True), the worker
    fell back to configure_account(load_settings().account), and
    that saw enabled=False -> 'Not configured', staying offline.
    Now the window saves the settings change before submitting,
    so the worker's load_settings() picks up enabled=True and a
    fresh REGISTER actually fires. The Account dialog also reports
    Enabled = on next time the user opens it, matching their
    intent of being online from now on.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Recording now waits for the call to be ANSWERED. Calls cancelled
    while ringing (487 Request Terminated) no longer leave a WAV +
    MP3 in ~/.local/share/gsipper/recordings. _maybe_start_recording
    is gated on STATE_CONNECTED; audio media that comes up during
    early media (183 Session Progress with SDP) is cached and the
    recorder is only created once onCallState reaches CONFIRMED.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix pjlib assertion ('Calling pjlib from unknown/external thread')
    crashing the app right after a recorded call ended. The
    AudioMediaRecorder ref was being dropped on the GTK main thread,
    so the SWIG-generated destructor invoked pjmedia cleanup off the
    pjsua2 worker. Both the call and recorder refs are now packaged
    into a no-op closure submitted to the worker after the 5-second
    grace period, so SWIG destructors run on a pjsua2-registered
    thread.
  * Fix AttributeError 'AudioMediaRecorder object has no attribute
    "delete"' — that method only exists on pj.Account. The recorder
    closes through Python refcount-driven destruction; the dedicated
    stop_recording() + take_recorder() now reflect that.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Disconnect now paints the headerbar dot red immediately. The
