gsipper (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Status dot becomes a Gtk.MenuButton with a state-dependent menu:
    Disconnect / Reconnect / Exit when online, Connect / Exit when
    offline. Reconnect is now a refresh REGISTER (calling
    setRegistration(True) on an already-registered account); the
    previous Disconnect-then-Reconnect pattern tripped
    pjsua2.Error because PJSIP rejects the second call while the
    un-REGISTER transaction is still settling.
  * Faster GUI startup. The 40 MB pjsua2 .so and the SipEndpoint
    singleton are imported / built on the next idle slot AFTER the
    window paints. The window, tray icon and shell-extension
    D-Bus property are visible in their initial state ("connecting"
    or "offline" depending on account configuration) from frame 1.

